<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <fullName>Button_Label__c</fullName>
    <defaultValue>&apos;Continue&apos;</defaultValue>
    <description>Drives the label of this page's primary forward action. In the linear runtime it sets the Next/Continue button text the respondent clicks to advance; on the effective final visible page the template-level Submit Button Label (or Review Page Button Label when the review screen is enabled) takes precedence when populated, with this field as the legacy fallback (#244). In Stages Mode it sets the start-step button label on this page's stage card when the stage status is Todo or Optional and unstarted (formTemplate.js startLabel logic), falling back to the Stages_Start_Step_Fallback custom label when blank. Restricted picklist; values resolve through getPicklistValues so the label is rendered through Salesforce Translation Workbench for locale-aware display. Default 'Continue'. The Form_Template trigger overrides the first auto-created page to 'Start Step' when the template is created in Stages Mode.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Choose the text for this page's main forward button: the Next/Continue button in the linear runtime, or the start-step button on the stage card in Stages Mode. Pick something action-oriented (Continue, Apply Now, Submit Application); the picklist values translate through Translation Workbench so respondents see them in their own language.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Button Label</label>
